### Obtaining the global omega estimate based on relative GTR branch lengths and nucleotide substitution biases
* Log(L) = -17516.70, AIC-c = 35801.66 (377 estimated parameters)
* 1 partition. Total tree length by partition (subs/site) 14.138
* non-synonymous/synonymous rate ratio for *test* =   0.8441

### Fitting Standard MG94
* Log(L) = -16543.14, AIC-c = 33864.93 (382 estimated parameters)
* non-synonymous/synonymous rate ratio =   1.0122
* The following relative rate distribution (mean 1) for site-to-site **non-synonymous** rate variation was inferred

|               Rate                | Proportion, % |               Notes               |
|-----------------------------------|---------------|-----------------------------------|
|               0.115               |    32.267     |                                   |
|               0.721               |    40.229     |                                   |
|               2.447               |    27.504     |                                   |


### Fitting MG94 with double instantaneous substitutions
* Log(L) = -16350.93, AIC-c = 33482.60 (383 estimated parameters)
* non-synonymous/synonymous rate ratio =   0.8649
* rate at which 2 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon =   0.3209
* The following relative rate distribution (mean 1) for site-to-site **non-synonymous** rate variation was inferred

|               Rate                | Proportion, % |               Notes               |
|-----------------------------------|---------------|-----------------------------------|
|               0.120               |    34.115     |                                   |
|               0.762               |    40.027     |                                   |
|               2.529               |    25.857     |                                   |


### Fitting MG94 with double and triple instantaneous substitutions
* Log(L) = -16346.61, AIC-c = 33476.04 (384 estimated parameters)
* non-synonymous/synonymous rate ratio =   0.8968
* rate at which 2 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon =   0.2918
* rate at which 3 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon =   0.1210
* rate at which 3 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon between synonymous codon islands =   0.1210
* The following relative rate distribution (mean 1) for site-to-site **non-synonymous** rate variation was inferred

|               Rate                | Proportion, % |               Notes               |
|-----------------------------------|---------------|-----------------------------------|
|               0.116               |    32.951     |                                   |
|               0.738               |    39.949     |                                   |
|               2.461               |    27.101     |                                   |


